// rbIsLambda is SHARED as rtHas - lib/runtime.metajs: an identity scan of an
// array, which is dart's dtSeen and php's phNameIn and, returning the index
// instead, rtDictFind. The array was a file global here rather than a parameter,
// which is the only reason three copies of it were invisible for so long.

// ===================================================== $globals =============

function rbGset(name, v) {
    rbGlobals["$" + name] = v
    rbGlobalNames["$" + name] = true
    return undefined
}

// ===================================================== the exports ==========
//
// Everything below is a TOP-LEVEL `function js_*`, which is what -rt-lib exports
// under its own C symbol. The language-NEUTRAL externs of abnf/jsrt.go come
// first, then Ruby's own, in the order of the extern table at the end of
// abnf/jsrt.go.

// ----- the language-NEUTRAL eight -------------------------------------------
// None of these is Ruby's. They live in abnf/jsrt.go, several languages emit
// them, and they are here only because the C floor does not have them yet.

// An empty Hash / Python dict / Go map handle.
// js_dict_new is SHARED - lib/runtime.metajs (six identical copies, no knobs).

// js_is_type is SHARED - lib/runtime.metajs, via the rtkIsChar/rtkIsArr hooks.
// The jsChar arm of the shared body is Kotlin's; rtkIsChar answers false here,
// because Ruby has no character type.
//
// js_jadd is SHARED - lib/runtime.metajs, via the rtkStr/rtkNum hooks above.
// The ruby emitter reaches it only for the internal loop counters it increments
// (js_jadd(i, 1)), never on a user value, so the shared float arm is dead here.

function rbJStr(v) {
    if (typeof v == "string") { return v }
    if (rbIsNil(v)) { return "null" }
    return "" + v
}

// A builtin exception instance for the Python pair. The ruby emitter uses it for
// its own control signals (the block-break and retry markers), which is why the
// class descriptor carries only __name.
function js_pyexc(name, args) {
